# Chapter 3 checkpoint. Start the app first:
#   dotnet run --project AdventureWorks
# (https://localhost:7001 and http://localhost:5001, Development).
# Chapter 2's User Secret FeatureFlags:MaxCartItems is 30.
# Each "Expect" line is the status you should see.

@host = https://localhost:7001

###
# The terminal MapWhen branch answers before the correlation
# middleware, so the response has no X-Correlation-ID header.
# Expect 200
GET {{host}}/ping

###
# A valid correlation ID is echoed, and the UseWhen branch marks
# /api responses. The response carries
# X-Correlation-ID: checkout-42 and carries X-API-Pipeline: true.
# Expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/status
X-Correlation-ID: checkout-42

###
# Order 1. Expect 200 with "orderNumber": "AW-0001"
GET {{host}}/api/orders/1

###
# DomainValidationException becomes Problem Details.
# Expect 400 with "title": "Invalid request"
GET {{host}}/api/orders/0

###
# ResourceNotFoundException becomes Problem Details with the
# correlation ID. Expect 404 with "title": "Resource not found"
GET {{host}}/api/orders/7

###
# The repository's simulated storage failure. Development shows
# the developer exception page. Expect 500
GET {{host}}/api/orders/500

###
# Status-code pages fill an empty 404. Expect 404
GET {{host}}/missing

###
# Chapter 1 and 2 routes still answer. Expect 302
# @no-redirect
GET {{host}}/

###
# Expect 200
GET {{host}}/health

###
# Expect 200 with "maxCartItems": 30
GET {{host}}/api/config

###
# Expect 200 with "isValid": true
GET {{host}}/api/email-check?address=ada@example.com
